About WPP Media

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence, and world-class partnerships - all united by our pioneering agentic marketing platform, WPP Open - we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity, and deliver transformational growth. 

WPP Media is WPP's AI-driven media operating unit, bringing together media, data, and partnerships to deliver creative personalisation at scale. Connected through WPP Open and powered by Open Intelligence, clients see exactly where, how, and why their media investment is working.

For more information, visit wppmedia.com .

Role Summary and Impact   &nbsp;

You will play a key role as a Media Planning Associate with a dynamic team focused on delivering best in class campaigns. You will get the opportunity to work together with other members of the Team across branding and performance across all channels.&nbsp;

Skills and Experience  &nbsp;

Responsibilities of the Role: &nbsp;

• Develop and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;relationships with clients, agency partners, and media partners.&nbsp;

• Work with the Manager on strategy development and idea generation for campaigns.&nbsp;

• Develop and present media plans/documents incorporating goals, recommendations, rationale, ideas, implementation, planning costs, and budget splits.&nbsp;

• Manage and deliver the day-to-day needs of the accounts.&nbsp;

• Develop and deliver necessary reports like media flowchart updates, budget updates, contact reports, competitive, post-campaign reports,&nbsp;in a timely manner.&nbsp;

• Manage negotiation, evaluation, and recommendation of media campaign proposals&nbsp;

• Adopt best practices around client structure, channel-wise understanding, media planning, and exposure to both offline and online tech partners.&nbsp;

• Be familiar with campaign processes (optimization, reporting, ways of working,&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;and billing).&nbsp;

• Work with the finance department to ensure all finance processes are adhered to and relevant data is updated.&nbsp;

In three months:  &nbsp;

• Be onboarded onto the account with full induction/training into all&nbsp;facets&nbsp;of the account.&nbsp;

• Adopt best practices around client structure, channel-wise understanding, media planning, and exposure to both offline and online tech partners.&nbsp;

• Be familiar with campaign processes (optimization, reporting, ways of working,&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;and billing).&nbsp;

• Demonstrate mastery of all platforms and systems which power media planning&nbsp;

• Work and collaborate closely with various internal specialist teams to ensure campaigns are managed from end-to-end&nbsp;ie&nbsp;Brief, Launch, Post Buys&nbsp;

In six months:  &nbsp;

• Confidently run the client account independently, meeting all KPIs, and assuming client relationship management.&nbsp;

• Become a trusted advisor through strong justification of recommendations, strong timeline management, and delivering outcomes.&nbsp;

• Drive the testing of new channels, formats, betas, platforms, and other innovations for our clients.&nbsp;

• Take on more client-facing responsibilities and get involved in weekly WIP meetings,&nbsp;attempting&nbsp;to educate and share new features and services.&nbsp;

• Assist&nbsp;the team in research, defining strategy to prepare presentation material.&nbsp;

In 12 months:  &nbsp;

• Build strong client relationships measured by feedback from Agency Scores.&nbsp;

• Independently be able to&nbsp;analyze&nbsp;and provide insights per channel,&nbsp;recommendations&nbsp;and next steps&nbsp;

What You Will Need: &nbsp;

• Minimally 1 year of media planning experience, preferably in a media agency and in a client-facing role.&nbsp;

• Up to date with industry changes and latest practices and procedures.&nbsp;

• Excellent administrative and organization skills.&nbsp;

• Strong attention to detail with&nbsp;high levels&nbsp;of accuracy.&nbsp;

